00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:09.000
Monday, February 22nd

00:02:09.290 --> 00:02:11.000
<i>Do you know what an affiliate blog is?</i>

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:13.510
Supernatural Science Kiri Kiri Basara

00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:15.260
<i>For you fellow NEETs out there,
no other job can be this wonderful.</i>

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:17.260
<i>Basically, if the popularity
of your blog goes up,</i>

00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:19.340
<i>of course the number
of site views goes up as well.</i>

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:23.520
<i>From there, more people will click on
the items on sale, and your income goes up.</i>

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:27.230
<i>Anyway, I am "NEET God," and the site I run,
"Supernatural Science Kiri Kiri Basara,"</i>

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:29.980
<i>picks up good articles
from news websites and personal blogs.</i>

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:33.900
<i>Then I make them brief, awesome, and
most importantly, stylish and easy to read.</i>

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:35.030
<i>It's an easy job.</i>

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:37.900
<i>In other words, I'm a normal NEET
in second year of high school</i>

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:42.740
<i>who's dreaming of increasing affiliate income
to get rich quick like a certain senpai.</i>

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:44.790
<i>But I don't make so much
that you'd get jealous.</i>

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:47.000
<i>It's such a disheartening amount
that it makes me want to die.</i>

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:49.420
<i>Since the occult is ridiculously
popular lately,</i>

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:51.920
<i>I made a round-up website like this,
but I may have been wrong.</i>

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:55.670
<i>On the other hand, similar sites appeared,
so I can't gain any site views at all.</i>

00:02:55.670 --> 00:03:01.260
<i>But my biggest goal is for all you Basarars
to provide me with fun stories to share.</i>

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:02.220
<i>Kiri!</i>

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:06.430
<i>I'm looking forward to those sharp points
of view from all you Basarars again!</i>

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:06.430
YUTA GAMON

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:13.690
<i>It's true that I'm an otaku and a virgin,
but I'm not creepy!</i>

00:03:13.690 --> 00:03:14.770
<i>If I dress normally,</i>

00:03:14.770 --> 00:03:17.190
<i>I'd say my looks are slightly better
than average in my class. I think.</i>

00:03:17.190 --> 00:03:18.650
Gamota...

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:20.950
even if your looks
were slightly better than average,

00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:23.740
if you bury the bottom half of your face
with a pathetic duffel coat

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:27.370
and mumble things to yourself,
that's totally ruining it!

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:31.920
Manager Izumin,
can I get a refill on my water?

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:34.460
Sheesh! Don't push me to work so hard!

00:03:35.170 --> 00:03:37.880
You know, Gamota,
what was that thing, Kiri Kiri Hag?

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:38.920
Kiri Kiri Basara.

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:40.630
I took a small peek at it, too.

00:03:40.630 --> 00:03:43.550
If you make fun of ghosts,
you'll be cursed someday!

00:03:43.550 --> 00:03:44.970
The occult really exists!

00:03:44.970 --> 00:03:46.470
Izumin won't help you out!

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:48.350
It's all on you!

00:03:48.350 --> 00:03:50.850
A curse? Makes me laugh!
There's no way there are any ghosts!

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:52.560
You know what, Manager Izumin?

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:54.770
Kiri Kiri Basara
isn't just a round-up website.

00:03:55.190 --> 00:03:57.690
It takes the many occultic supernatural
phenomena that exist in the world

00:03:56.270 --> 00:03:56.780
You can see something like a face?
Then it's a ghost photograph.

00:03:56.780 --> 00:03:57.280
Curse of Kokkuri is seriously scary!

00:03:57.280 --> 00:03:58.280
A girl lived with a mummy dude? Seriously?

00:03:57.690 --> 00:04:01.910
and refutes them down drastically
with slicing points of view in a funny way!

00:04:01.910 --> 00:04:04.910
I named the site this in a fit of rage,
but I don't regret it at all.

00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:07.370
For you see, the Basarars
that write stuff in are more fierce

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:07.370
Raining, pouring, splish splash!

00:04:07.370 --> 00:04:09.870
with their slicing points of view
than I am.

00:04:07.370 --> 00:04:14.710
Ribbit, ribbit!
It's Gamotan who's croaking!

00:04:09.870 --> 00:04:12.500
If anything, I have to say
this is nothing but me being lucky.

00:04:14.710 --> 00:04:15.710
RYOKA NARUSAWA

00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:22.510
Gamotan croaks, ribbit, ribbit, ribbit!

00:04:22.510 --> 00:04:23.260
I don't croak.

00:04:23.260 --> 00:04:24.760
-Gamotan! Ribbitan!
-Yes.

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:31.100
Gamotan! Ribbitan! Gamotan! Ribbitan!

00:04:27.850 --> 00:04:31.100
Stop! Yeah, yeah, stop dancing!

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:32.100
Huh?

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:33.270
No time for "Huh."

00:04:33.270 --> 00:04:37.320
Well, Ryo-tas, your job isn't that of a dancer
but a staff member of Kiri Kiri Basara.

00:04:37.480 --> 00:04:38.900
You need to go look
for stories together with me—

00:04:40.030 --> 00:04:43.360
- Ishishu it is!
- Hold, stop it, Ryo-tas! Poya-gun! No!

00:04:41.700 --> 00:04:43.360
What should I be doing here?

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:45.320
Everything is okay!
Everything is okay just like this!

00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:48.160
One year behind me in Seimei High school,
this is Ryoka Narusawa, a.k.a. Ryo-tas!

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:50.040
I'm so cool because I'm friends
with a girl like this!

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:53.120
Truly fulfilled in real life!
So everything is okay! But, no!

00:04:53.420 --> 00:04:55.290
Poya-gun! No!

00:04:54.420 --> 00:04:55.290
You know?

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:59.300
Kiri Kiri Basara was a blog just for
"Operation Gamotan Gets Rich," right?

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:00.670
But even if Ryo-tas helps out,

00:05:00.670 --> 00:05:03.050
that has nothing to do
with the Operation Get Rich part, right?

00:05:03.050 --> 00:05:06.180
Th-Then, if I get some income from
the affiliate, I'll treat you to some Staton.

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:08.430
I'd personally recommend
the soy sauce and garlic.

00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:10.390
Oh, would you prefer
the salt and garlic instead?

00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:10.390
STATON

00:05:11.270 --> 00:05:15.270
Ryo-tas would prefer Woodberrries
frozen yogurt instead of that.

00:05:15.270 --> 00:05:16.520
W-Woodberrie...

00:05:15.770 --> 00:05:16.520
WOODBERRIES FROZEN YOGURT

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:20.440
It's a shop that specializes
in frozen yogurt near the train station.

00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:21.530
I-I see.

00:05:21.530 --> 00:05:22.490
Then we'll go with that.

00:05:22.490 --> 00:05:26.450
Hey, hey, when will Ryo-tas
be able to eat some frozen yogurt?

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:26.450
S-So close!

00:05:26.450 --> 00:05:28.910
W-Well, whenever I get some money
from the affiliate, I guess.

00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:32.370
So Ryo-tas, can you put away
that super-dangerous Poya-gun now?

00:05:32.830 --> 00:05:35.250
Then, I'll check up
on the number of site views.

00:05:37.210 --> 00:05:38.540
The monthly total is...

00:05:40.130 --> 00:05:41.550
So my luck is strong after all!

00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:44.010
But no, God controls all things in life!

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:46.970
There will be a day
when the occult overpasses even Eros!

00:05:47.220 --> 00:05:49.890
God is "Ero"him Essaim!

00:05:50.220 --> 00:05:52.390
<i>Proving the existence
of spirits with science...</i>

00:05:52.390 --> 00:05:54.180
PROFESSOR
KANSEI HASHIGAMI

00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:55.230
<i>Either that act will be the biggest
embarrassment of the century,</i>

00:05:55.230 --> 00:05:57.770
or you will end up
as the Galileo of the 21st century.

00:05:58.020 --> 00:06:03.400
Whichever it may end up, I believe
it is the mission of all scientists to pursue it.

00:05:58.150 --> 00:05:59.150
PSYCHIC
SHIZUKO KIMURA

00:05:59.150 --> 00:06:02.150
SCIENCE JOURNALIST
TAKAHIKO SAWAZAKI

00:05:59.150 --> 00:06:02.150
POP IDOL
AMAKO UTSUMI

00:06:02.150 --> 00:06:11.910
SPECIAL PROGRAM
OCCULTIC SCIENCE LAB

00:06:03.940 --> 00:06:05.950
Mr. Hashigami, you are
a formal member of the SPR,

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:09.990
Society for Psychical Research, correct?

00:06:10.240 --> 00:06:12.450
I hear that you are the only
Japanese member of the society.

00:06:12.450 --> 00:06:14.950
Yes. It is an organization
to promote scientific research

00:06:14.950 --> 00:06:17.580
of poltergeists
and supernatural phenomena.

00:06:17.830 --> 00:06:21.880
It was organized in 1882
at Trinity College of Cambridge University.

00:06:22.130 --> 00:06:24.670
Jung, Freud and Lewis Carroll
were members, as well.

00:06:24.670 --> 00:06:27.130
The fact that SPR is an organization
with a long history

00:06:27.130 --> 00:06:29.590
is something
all scientists will agree to.

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:33.390
However, the prime days of the organization
were well over a century ago, correct?

00:06:33.390 --> 00:06:36.390
In the 21st century
with all the technological advances,

00:06:36.390 --> 00:06:39.600
the society is being pushed away
from academia, correct?

00:06:39.770 --> 00:06:41.480
It indeed may be that way.

00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:45.610
But overseas, there are many scientists
who are serious about this subject.

00:06:45.610 --> 00:06:47.110
You say that,

00:06:47.110 --> 00:06:52.120
but not one university in Japan
allows you to learn parapsychology!

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:52.830
Right.

00:06:52.830 --> 00:06:55.120
For example,
souls of the dead do not exist.

00:06:55.370 --> 00:06:58.330
That existence has been denied
in many fields of science.

00:06:58.330 --> 00:07:02.090
History like that has created the foundation
for modern-day technology, correct?

00:07:02.090 --> 00:07:04.000
Mr. Hashigami, would you beg to differ?

00:07:04.250 --> 00:07:08.130
There is no concrete proof
that souls do not materially exist, either.

00:07:08.130 --> 00:07:11.760
I am sick and tired of science
ignoring strange events.

00:07:12.470 --> 00:07:13.850
Listen up, everyone.

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:16.270
Souls do indeed exist.

00:07:17.480 --> 00:07:19.230
Spiritual!

00:07:20.270 --> 00:07:24.570
Ms. Utsumi, how did you interpret
Mr. Hashigami's talk just now?

00:07:24.730 --> 00:07:27.320
I don't get it too well,

00:07:27.570 --> 00:07:32.530
but aren't the cuticles
of Mr. Hashigami's hair amazing?

00:07:32.780 --> 00:07:35.790
Cuticle, curl, curl!

00:07:34.990 --> 00:07:37.700
I'm amazed that he'd actually
be on shows like this.

00:07:37.700 --> 00:07:40.040
He's totally aware
they're going to bash on him, too.

00:07:40.040 --> 00:07:42.580
Maybe he likes showing himself
in front of people?

00:07:52.340 --> 00:07:54.010
This is such a farce.

00:07:58.020 --> 00:07:58.980
It's a waste of time.

00:07:58.980 --> 00:07:59.980
SARAI HASHIGAMI

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:03.230
<i>Do you just want to show off?</i>

00:08:03.230 --> 00:08:05.610
<i>Or do you really
want to unravel poltergeists?</i>

00:08:06.360 --> 00:08:07.610
<i>Which is it, Dad?</i>

00:08:07.860 --> 00:08:08.780
<i>Hurry!</i>

00:08:09.150 --> 00:08:12.280
<i>Please, Sarai! You need to hurry up
and speak with your father!</i>

00:08:17.990 --> 00:08:20.460
NOTICE
Professor Hashigami's Introduction to Science
and Engineering lecture has been cancelled.

00:08:22.790 --> 00:08:24.960
Was he eaten by a demon?

00:08:26.290 --> 00:08:30.590
Or is he about to get eaten?

00:08:31.170 --> 00:08:32.180
RIRIKA NISHIZONO

00:08:37.560 --> 00:08:38.560
A demon?

00:08:41.940 --> 00:08:42.560
MONTHLY MUMU

00:08:41.940 --> 00:08:42.560
EDITORIAL DIVISION 3

00:08:43.560 --> 00:08:46.150
<i>Though, if I were to reword it
in scientific jargon...</i>

00:08:44.810 --> 00:08:46.690
I'm back now!

00:08:51.030 --> 00:08:51.950
Thanks for the hard work.

00:08:53.110 --> 00:08:54.110
TOUKO SUMIKAZE

00:08:54.450 --> 00:08:56.120
Thanks for the hard work,
Editor-in-Chief.

00:08:56.120 --> 00:08:59.540
That's the next manuscript
for Mr. Hashigami. It's looking good.

00:08:59.990 --> 00:09:01.540
You've already read it?

00:09:01.540 --> 00:09:03.750
Who do you think picked it up from him?

00:09:03.750 --> 00:09:05.380
It wasn't Makabe?

00:09:05.380 --> 00:09:06.630
It was me! Me!

00:09:06.880 --> 00:09:08.590
The editor-in-chief directly went?

00:09:09.840 --> 00:09:12.010
So, what in the world
is about to begin now?

00:09:12.260 --> 00:09:15.090
Will there be an UFO invasion
from the Large Magellanic Cloud tomorrow?

00:09:15.090 --> 00:09:16.430
There won't be.

00:09:16.430 --> 00:09:17.680
If such a thing were to happen,

00:09:17.680 --> 00:09:20.270
I'd already have gotten information
long ago from an acquaintance.

00:09:20.270 --> 00:09:22.560
I mean, I have connections
all over the world.

00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:24.440
I was just joking around.

00:09:24.690 --> 00:09:28.360
You're a mature adult now, you don't
have to act so proud about things like that!

00:09:28.690 --> 00:09:32.610
Anyways, that aside, I just needed
to head to Kichijoji this morning.

00:09:32.610 --> 00:09:36.240
So I thought I'd drop by Mr. Hashigami's
place since I was all the way out there.

00:09:36.240 --> 00:09:37.950
Thank you for all that trouble.

00:09:37.950 --> 00:09:38.740
Yeah.

00:09:38.740 --> 00:09:41.040
If Mr. Hashigami would get a computer,

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:44.040
we wouldn't have to go get
manuscripts from him anymore.

00:09:42.750 --> 00:09:46.120
<i>The data stored within the human brain
is released outside the body after death</i>

00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:45.420
Oh, don't say that.

00:09:45.420 --> 00:09:48.420
They say that the author's will resides
within handwritten manuscripts.

00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:48.420
<i>as magnetic data with its own will.</i>

00:09:48.420 --> 00:09:49.380
<i>The real guise of the ghost is—</i>

00:09:48.420 --> 00:09:50.500
Can that be something occultic?

00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:50.500
<i>Calm it down!</i>

00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:52.010
It's a policy. My policy.

00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:53.880
<i>There are many evil demons
and evil spirits here!</i>

00:09:52.460 --> 00:09:53.880
By the way, Sumikaze...

00:09:54.130 --> 00:09:55.970
is Mr. Hashigami a misanthrope?

00:09:56.510 --> 00:09:57.590
What do you mean by that?

00:09:57.590 --> 00:09:59.640
Well, when I went
to pick up the manuscript...

00:10:00.680 --> 00:10:02.810
<i>Here is the manuscript.</i>

00:10:02.810 --> 00:10:04.020
<i>Thank you very much.</i>

00:10:04.480 --> 00:10:06.940
<i>Um, is Mr. Hashigami out?</i>

00:10:06.940 --> 00:10:08.900
<i>No, he is home now.</i>

00:10:09.110 --> 00:10:11.860
Mr. Hashigami's mother? Not his wife?

00:10:11.860 --> 00:10:12.650
Yeah.

00:10:12.900 --> 00:10:15.610
It seemed like she was
at least 70 years old.

00:10:15.610 --> 00:10:19.910
I thought Mr. Hashigami's mother
had deceased quite a while ago.

00:10:20.160 --> 00:10:21.790
This is an episode of his series
from last year.

00:10:22.040 --> 00:10:24.120
He talks about his late mother in it.

00:10:24.370 --> 00:10:28.710
You're right. But the one that greeted me
was most definitely an old woman.

00:10:28.710 --> 00:10:29.790
Maybe...

00:10:31.460 --> 00:10:32.800
it was a ghost?

00:10:34.090 --> 00:10:35.880
That's the best!

00:10:35.880 --> 00:10:38.300
I've been a writer for Mumu
for 30 years now,

00:10:38.300 --> 00:10:41.220
but I can't tell the difference
between a real person and a ghost!

00:10:41.550 --> 00:10:44.560
There's a lot more to the world
than meets the eye!

00:10:44.560 --> 00:10:47.060
That wasn't necessarily a joke, though.

00:10:47.440 --> 00:10:47.850
MUMU

00:10:48.400 --> 00:10:51.900
A girl lived with a mummy dude? Seriously?

00:10:48.730 --> 00:10:52.940
Man, won't there be some miraculous
increase in site views?

00:10:52.940 --> 00:10:55.780
What do we do for a miraculous
increase to happen?

00:10:56.030 --> 00:10:59.610
Maybe we can ask someone famous
to make an appearance. Like that guy.

00:10:59.610 --> 00:11:01.530
Then all you have to do is negotiate!

00:11:01.530 --> 00:11:03.200
That's so cumbersome,
too cumbersome.

00:11:03.200 --> 00:11:06.200
Hey guys, I'm changing channels to watch
"Your Loss If You Don't Know POM!"

00:11:06.200 --> 00:11:07.830
<i>The internet is in an uproar!</i>

00:11:06.200 --> 00:11:11.210
Your Loss If You Don't Know POM!

00:11:07.830 --> 00:11:11.210
<i>We'll be showing the high school girl
fortune-teller Miyuu Aikawa!</i>

00:11:12.290 --> 00:11:13.880
It's Miyuu!

00:11:13.880 --> 00:11:16.300
Oh, you know her, Gamota?
Is she your girlfriend?

00:11:16.670 --> 00:11:19.380
Miyuu is making her
network TV debut on "Dunno POM"?

00:11:19.380 --> 00:11:22.010
This is truly a Myu-pom!
I think this is gonna go viral!

00:11:22.010 --> 00:11:24.060
Oh, is this from Inokashira Park?

00:11:24.060 --> 00:11:26.310
I wonder if she lives close to Kichijoji?

00:11:27.020 --> 00:11:30.980
Yep, just right! Even watching it on digital
groundwave, she's just right after all?

00:11:30.230 --> 00:11:30.980
Huh?

00:11:30.980 --> 00:11:32.810
I've seen this girl around our school.

00:11:32.810 --> 00:11:33.610
Seriously?

00:11:33.820 --> 00:11:36.030
<i>Please let me see your vision.</i>

00:11:36.030 --> 00:11:37.030
MIYUU AIKAWA

00:11:43.490 --> 00:11:45.870
You really are the Kurenaino Aria?

00:11:46.120 --> 00:11:48.040
You seem rather young.

00:11:48.330 --> 00:11:50.120
I really am. Is there
something wrong with that?

00:11:49.120 --> 00:11:50.120
KURENAINO ARIA

00:11:50.120 --> 00:11:52.290
I see. Then, nothing is wrong.

00:11:52.670 --> 00:11:54.130
What's your request?

00:11:56.500 --> 00:11:58.720
I'd like you to curse
a certain man to death.

00:11:59.090 --> 00:12:02.390
In order to perform black magic,
I need something to act as a catalyst.

00:12:02.390 --> 00:12:03.600
Do you have something on hand?

00:12:08.520 --> 00:12:09.480
For certain.

00:12:12.980 --> 00:12:17.440
Then, please enter the information
